## Jev client origin

The Jev client in `bin/jev_review.py`, `bin/jev_plan.py`, and
`bin/jev_triage.py` is project code, not a vendor SDK. It targets a
typed-question HTTP interface and does not include model weights, model files,
or a hosted service.

`JEV_ENDPOINT` points at an external inference service. The service, its
availability, its terms, and its billing are separate from this repository. No
service credential or model is distributed here.

## Dependency boundary

Nothing in this list is bundled in the repository.

| Dependency | Role | Distribution |
|---|---|---|
| OpenCode | The host application that loads agents, commands, skills, and plugins | Installed by the user, separate project |
| `@opencode-ai/plugin` | Development dependency for plugin types and tests | Not bundled; license and version per upstream package |
| Jev inference endpoint | External service called by the Jev client | Not bundled; separate service and terms |
| Provider models | Models selected by the user in OpenCode or by `JEV_MODEL` | Not bundled; separate provider terms |
| External npm plugins named in user configuration | Optional user-installed plugins | Not bundled, not endorsed, and not supported |

The Python code uses the standard library only. The bundled Node plugins use
Node built-ins only. See `package.json` for the development dependency version.

